+## CI/CD Architecture — End of Sprint 4
+
+### Workflow Files
+
+| Workflow | File | Trigger | What it runs |
+|----------|------|---------|--------------|
+| Python CI | `.github/workflows/python-app.yml` | Every PR (not on merge) | One job: ruff → mypy → unit tests (`pytest -m "not ui"`) → start Flask → API tests → stop Flask |
+| Playwright UI Tests | `.github/workflows/playwright.yml` | PR to main + `workflow_dispatch` | Install Chromium → start Flask → `pytest -m ui` → stop Flask |
+
+### Why Two Workflows?
+`python-app.yml` must be fast — it runs on every PR. Playwright tests require
+Chromium installation and a running Flask server — adding them would add 2–3 minutes
+to every PR's main check. Separate workflows keep fast feedback fast, and each
+shows as its own check on the PR. Both workflows run on PRs only and skip
+image/docs-only changes (S4_1 CI Pipeline Tune-Up).
+
+### Pipeline Hardening (closes the S3_2 CI finding)
+
+| Safeguard | Where | Why |
+|-----------|-------|-----|
+| `setup-uv` pinned to `version: "0.13.0"` | Both workflows | Permanent fix for environment drift — uv only changes when the team changes the number through a PR |
+| `Stop Flask server` with `if: always()` | Both workflows | Teardown — every job that starts a server stops it, even when a test step fails (immediate fix from S3_2, now applied to `playwright.yml` too) |
+
+Everything that can drift is now pinned: Python packages (`uv.lock`), Python (`python-version: "3.13"`), and uv itself.
+
+### pytest Markers
+- `@pytest.mark.ui` — Playwright browser tests
+- Defined in `pyproject.toml` → `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` → `markers`
+
+## Tool Configuration — pyproject.toml (Complete as of S4_3)
+
+`pytest.ini` deleted in S4_3. All tool configuration now in `pyproject.toml`.
+
+| Tool | Section | Key Settings |
+|------|---------|--------------|
+| mypy | `[tool.mypy]` | `disallow_untyped_defs`, `exclude` |
+| ruff | `[tool.ruff]` | `line-length = 88`, `target-version` |
+| ruff lint | `[tool.ruff.lint]` | `select = ["E", "F", "W", "I"]` |
+| bandit | `[tool.bandit]` | `exclude_dirs` — read only with `-c pyproject.toml`; path stays on the CLI (`-r app/`) |
+| pytest | `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` | `pythonpath`, `testpaths`, `addopts`, `markers` |
+
+Single source of truth: one file, one syntax, consistent across terminal and CI.
+
+### Dependency Removed — S4_3
+
+| Package | Decision | Reason |
+|---------|----------|--------|
+| `robotframework-browser` | Removed from dev dependencies | No test imports it; its init step required Node.js, which the project does not use. S5_2 Robot tests use `RequestsLibrary`. |
+
+Rule applied: every dependency must have a consumer — a test that imports it, a tool that reads it, or a CI step that runs it. Entries without one are removed.
